  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Flight Route Map\n\nA plane flies a glowing route between two labelled pins over a drawn map, the camera drifts, the destination gets a hand-drawn circle and an arrival badge.\n\nCategory: motion-graphics. Length: 6 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A journey from one place to another needs to read at a glance: a trip, a delivery, an expansion.\n- The scene is an opener or a transition card with a headline.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The map must show real geography: this draws an abstract map.\n- You need more than two stops.\n\nVariables:\n- origin (string): Origin, default \"Harbor City\"\n- origin_code (string): Origin code, default \"HBR / NORTH\"\n- destination (string): Destination, default \"Summit City\"\n- destination_code (string): Destination code, default \"SMT / EAST\"\n- eyebrow (string): Eyebrow, default \"Six-second hop\"\n- joiner (string): Joiner, default \"TO\"\n- route_note (string): Route note, default \"A long way, compressed\"\n- arrived (string): Arrival badge, default \"ARRIVED\"\n- accent (color): Route colour, default \"#2563eb\"\n- doodle (color): Circle colour, default \"#e5322d\"\n- ink (color): Text colour, default \"#1d1d1f\"\n- ocean (color): Ocean, default \"#dfe7f1\"\n- land (color): Land, default \"#f6f6f2\"\n\nSource: heygen-com/hyperframes. Licence: Apache-2.0. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
